WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.340
This is Quinten and Jef, and they turned a family tradition into a platform that has raised 1.3

00:05.340 --> 00:10.400
million euros for charity. This idea started together with my dad. He already has the Parkinson's

00:10.400 --> 00:15.460
disease for 15 years. Every hospital checkup I sent him a message with, I'm lighting a candle

00:15.460 --> 00:19.580
for you to wish you good luck. He came up with the idea, what if he could light a candle with

00:19.580 --> 00:24.040
a phone and at the same time could raise money for the Parkinson's disease. To bring it to life,

00:24.040 --> 00:29.080
Quinten called his longtime friend Jef. Quinten and I spoke for the first time through gym class,

00:29.080 --> 00:35.340
and it was like the, you know, the typical Spider-Man meme where, like, you're meeting the exact same type of guy.

00:35.520 --> 00:37.320
Together, they started building WeGlow.

00:37.500 --> 00:41.380
And over the next five years, they spoke to every nonprofit in Belgium and the Netherlands.

00:41.760 --> 00:45.520
The more people they spoke to, the more they learned, and the bigger the problem became.

00:45.820 --> 00:47.520
Nonprofits have two options.

00:47.860 --> 00:52.240
Super expensive SaaS, where they pay thousands of euros every year.

00:52.440 --> 00:56.500
Or they have, like, free platforms where they aren't the owner of the donor data

00:56.500 --> 00:59.620
and they don't receive the donations right through their bank account.

00:59.760 --> 01:01.180
We really saw a big problem there.

01:01.420 --> 01:06.340
So our nice idea of lighting a candle and the big nonprofit problem, we combined it.

01:06.520 --> 01:08.160
But WeGlow wasn't built overnight.

01:08.460 --> 01:09.920
Well, not initially.

01:10.240 --> 01:13.940
We spent a lot of money and we spent a lot of cash into trying to build that software.

01:14.120 --> 01:15.460
And it took us a lot of time.

01:15.620 --> 01:20.540
It was a very hard time, because we had a big dream, but we didn't have, like, the funds to

01:20.540 --> 01:22.920
invest in, like, a developer team.

01:22.920 --> 01:27.420
But our mission was so bright, and we had so much passion to, to

01:27.420 --> 01:32.040
launch this platform. And in one day I made everything we already had on WeGlow,

01:32.040 --> 01:36.600
where we built it for years. We had it in one day on Lovable. We are free, or

01:36.600 --> 01:40.300
really low cost, and all the money will go directly to your bank account, and you

01:40.300 --> 01:46.220
are also the owner of the donor data. We cover everything: donations, CRM, WeGlow

01:46.220 --> 01:51.060
mail, even newsletters. We can do everything that a nonprofit needs to start in digital fundraising.

01:51.060 --> 01:53.680
What started as a tradition between father and son

01:53.680 --> 01:56.140
could now be shared by millions across the world.

01:56.380 --> 01:59.720
The growth we had last year, it's something we dreamed of.

02:00.260 --> 02:03.980
We lighted more than 35,000 candles, raised more than 1.3 million.

02:04.160 --> 02:09.740
We've seen so many great campaigns, from people doing 100-kilometer runs

02:10.400 --> 02:14.320
from one point to another, to people cycling across Europe.

02:14.440 --> 02:18.340
For my dad to see all these campaigns coming up, he's super proud.

02:18.620 --> 02:21.560
Like, he really sent me and Jef a message with,

02:21.560 --> 02:23.200
so nice for you guys.

02:23.320 --> 02:24.480
I'm so proud of you guys.

02:24.680 --> 02:28.140
So for him, it's also a dream, just his idea to see it in reality.

02:28.880 --> 02:30.100
It's amazing to see.
